WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.183
(percussive music)

00:00:01.183 --> 00:00:02.240
- [Narrator] Vinegar is one of the oldest

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.150
fermented foods in the world,

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:07.163
but these days it seems to
be having a bit of a moment.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:11.500
In the town of Kagoshima in Japan,

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:14.060
you will find a special dark vinegar

00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.133
that has long been ahead of the times.

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.800
- [Announcer] This Great
Big Story is inspired by

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:21.633
Genesis.

00:00:22.915 --> 00:00:25.582
(lyrical music)

00:00:32.068 --> 00:00:35.985
(speaks in a foreign language)

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:47.860
- [Narrator] Tadaaki
is the brewmaster here

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:50.062
at the Sakamoto Jouzu Brewery.

00:00:50.062 --> 00:00:53.979
(speaks in a foreign language)

00:01:11.774 --> 00:01:14.790
(bouncy music)

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:17.830
The vinegar ferments in
special vases called tsubos

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:19.214
for over a year.

00:01:19.214 --> 00:01:23.131
(speaks in a foreign language)

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:35.130
This aging process is
what separates kurozu

00:01:35.130 --> 00:01:36.560
from other vinegars.

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.010
The longer the vinegar ferments

00:01:38.010 --> 00:01:39.430
the darker it will become,

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:41.699
and the smoother it will taste.

00:01:41.699 --> 00:01:45.616
(speaks in a foreign language)

00:02:08.676 --> 00:02:11.435
In Kagoshima you can also
find vinegar smoothies,

00:02:11.435 --> 00:02:12.340
(speaks in a foreign language)

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:14.450
soups, drinks, sauces,

00:02:14.450 --> 00:02:16.350
people can't seem to get enough of it.

00:02:17.943 --> 00:02:19.140
(quiet music)

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:21.990
Tadaaki has been a brewmaster
since he was 40 years old,

00:02:21.990 --> 00:02:24.743
and for him, the job can't be beat.

00:02:24.743 --> 00:02:28.660
(speaks in a foreign language)

00:02:49.543 --> 00:02:51.710
(chiming)

